e various samples  we also saw that the tumors in the  immune depleted subset  uh were distributed across the various  uh  tnbc subgroups so addition in addition  to pam-50  that does the initial subtyping the  panel also includes additional  triple negative breast cancer subtypes  and we see that these subtypes do not  necessarily predict  immune hot or cold tumors which is  definitely of interest because we know  that  some types of breast cancer predict  quite a bit of the biology of those  tumors  however in our results we saw that there  were a number of key immune markers  associated  with regression free survival in these  patients  first ido1 pdl1 and pdl2  all genes in the tumor signaling 360  panel  were significantly associated with  regression free survival and the  patients treated with capocitabine  and we also some some additional markers  associated with  improved regression-free survival in  these patients  and that included the endothelial cell  signature and the mast cell signature  again the mast cell signature is present  in the tumor signaling 360 panel as well  and so in summary the tumor signaling  360 panel  was designed to look at the  comprehensive biology behind the tumor  the tumor micro environment and the  immune response focusing  on tumor biology and primed for studies  investigating targeted therapeutics our  other 360 panels have already  and as you have seen shown great promise  and uncovering mechanisms of resistance  to various targeted therapies and we  look forward to the kinds of studies and  data that will be produced  on our new tumor signaling 360 panel  with that i'll thank you for your  attention and take any questions  thank you very much dr piazza for a very  informative presentation  few questions for you also  which of the 360 series  panel that um nanostring has  would be best suited for um  the study of a mythological malignancy  great question are our 360 panels  generally think  about those three areas of biology  tumor microenvironment and immune  response primarily in the context of  solid tumors where  there is a solid tumor micro environment  however in some uh some hematological  malignancies like  lymphomas there may actually be a solid  tumor micro environment  um and so in that case we we think that  the pan cancer io 360 panel  is the best panel especially because it  focuses primarily on the immune response  and the immune biology and tumor biology  in those tumors  is intricately linked however in some  hematological malignancies particularly  in leukemia  um it it would be worth taking a look at  our pan cancer immune profiling panel  that focuses pretty much solely on the  immune response  and would be an excellent choice for  looking at the comprehensive biology of  hematological malignancies especially in  cases without  a solid tumor micro environment per se  thank you can one receive a 360 data  analysis report  with the tumor signaling 360 panel  like for other of your panels  great question as well uh so for  the the 360 panels both paint cancer io  360  and breast cancer 360 have a specific  data analysis report  we did not produce one of these data  analysis reports specifically for tumor  signaling 360  and that's because we believe that the  biology of that panel was well  served by our existing pathway analysis  however in the case of people who want  to assess the tumor inflammation  signature  there is a specific analysis report that  can be generated  just for that signature and that is  something that is  is uh compatible with our tumor  signaling 360 panel  thank you how does the content  from the tumor signal in 360 panel  aligned with the content in the  cancer transcriptome atlas that is  available  through the geomets  the cancer transcriptome atlas is truly  an exciting new product  one that i'm very much looking forward  to seeing  increasing amounts of data on it  definitely covers very similar biology  uh to the tumor signaling 360 panel and  as such there is quite a bit  of overlap in the content of uh both of  those products  so um certainly if you're interested in  tumor signaling 360 panel please take a  look  at a cancer transcriptome atlas for dsp  geomics we very much look forward to uh  studies potentially on  on paired samples from both of those  soon  thank you does this panel  need a standard for the calculation of  the humor inflammation score  yes it does the tumor inflammation  signature  um does require a panel standard  that panel standard can be used also for  for batch calibration and longitudinal  studies  but certainly is required for accurate  test calculation  thank you how does the nano string  data analysis software work  our nano string data analysis software  starts in end solver  end solver is a relatively simple tool  that reads  in the proprietary data analysis formats  that come off of our instruments and  puts genes into a format that then can  be  transferred to our more advanced  analysis software  that software is written in r and has  a unique wizard tool that you can use to  select  some various options for your analysis  it imports the data from end solver and  then  with the parameters given generates  pathway scoring  cell type profiling gene set analysis  differential expression analysis and  many other  helpful figures  thank you again dr erin for the talk and  the discussion  this concludes the program for the  biomarker discovery track  thank you again to all the speakers for  their informative presentation and  discussion  as a reminder the speaker will follow up  with any question you have submitted  the i made and i want to thank you all  for  your participation


